			"notes": "Boosted Brightness v2 is packed with features! It is available for 1.17 and 1.16.4/5.\n\n## Up to 5 Custom Brightness Levels!\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/43352940/122160522-15903a80-ce3e-11eb-86f0-daa53a3b4788.png)\n- By default, there are 2 brightness levels: current brightness and 1200%\n- Add up to 3 additional brightness levels - e.g. super-dark, super-bright, cave-brightness, night-brightness\n- Sliders are accessed through [Mod Menu](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/modmenu)\n- The brightness slider in Video Settings now changes the currently selected brightness\n\n## Overlays!\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/43352940/122160981-e1694980-ce3e-11eb-9027-b53884120b77.png)\n- Shows your current brightness level in-game when changed using keybinds\n\n## Keybinds to Select Brightness Levels!\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/43352940/122161054-02ca3580-ce3f-11eb-81f3-1f623548b3fd.png)\n- Use keybinds to select particular brightness levels\n- By default, the keybinds to select particular brightness levels are unbound\n- If you have two brightness levels, the \"Select Next Brightness\" works just like the old brightness toggle\n\n## Other Minor Changes\n- Boosted Brightness now makes a config file `.minecraft/config/boostedbrightness.json`. The minimum (-100%) and maximum (1200%) along with all other values (step-size of raise/lower keybinds, 5 brightness levels, currently selected brightness level) are customizable here\n- Brightness sliders now update in increments of 5\n- [Mod Menu](https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/modmenu) is now required"
		},
